- op: create  # 2e03
  at: '2026-06-06T04:14:27Z'  # 2e03
  by: agent  # 2e03
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2e03
  clock: 1  # 2e03
  nonce: '2e03'  # 2e03
  data:  # 2e03
    kind: work_item  # 2e03
    title: "node.id trailing kind-segment disagrees with node.kind field on 1670 nodes; 8 starlette routes carry id-kind ':route' but kind-field 'function'"  # 2e03
    status: todo_hard  # 2e03
    priority: 2  # 2e03
    parent:  # 2e03
    tags:  # 2e03
    - dogfood  # 2e03
    - dogfood_tranche_05  # 2e03
    isbefore: []  # 2e03
    duplicate_of: []  # 2e03
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2e03
    pr_ref:  # 2e03
    description: "The documented node.id format is lang:path:span:name:kind, so the trailing colon segment IS the kind. But 1670 nodes have an id whose trailing segment differs from the actual kind field. (idkind, kindfield) pairs: unresolved->external_symbol 1312, attribute->external_symbol 214, doc_link->external_symbol 106, module->external_symbol 11, route->function 8, event_subscriber->function 11, event_publisher->function 3, npm_package->package 2, script->external_symbol 1, package->external_symbol 1, tsconfig->file 1. The external_symbol rows are arguably expected (id encodes reference syntax, kind normalizes to external_symbol); the route->function, event_subscriber->function, event_publisher->function rows are real producer disagreements where the id segment encodes a role the kind field does not carry. The 8 starlette route nodes (origin=['python'], a real analyzer NOT a linker) sit at route-REGISTRATION lines (span 428-428 etc.), separate from the actual handler-function nodes (serve.py:141-168, span 141-168) that the 8 http_route entrypoints correctly point to (0 of 8 entrypoint symbol_ids are :route nodes). Each starlette route is represented by TWO nodes — the handler function (referenced by the entrypoint) and a synthetic registration-line node with id-kind=route/kind-field=function/name='starlette:<handler>'. Fresh repro: hypergumbo run on a copy of serve.py -> 8 :route nodes, all kind=function. Consequence: a consumer parsing node.id per the documented ...:kind format gets 'route' while a consumer reading node.kind gets 'function' — the two disagree for 1670 nodes."  # 2e03
    fields: {}  # 2e03
- op: discuss  # 031b
