    title: "node.id kind-slot disagrees with node.kind on ~1645 external_symbol nodes (reference-syntax normalization, arguably-expected; route/event role-disagreement split to WI-kugaj)"  # f646
    description: "node.id's trailing colon segment is the documented kind, but on ~1645 nodes the id kind-slot disagrees with node.kind: unresolved->external_symbol 1312, attribute->external_symbol 214, doc_link->external_symbol 106, module->external_symbol 11, script->external_symbol 1, package->external_symbol 1, plus npm_package->package 2 and tsconfig->file 1 as a small non-external_symbol remainder. For the external_symbol rows this is arguably-EXPECTED: the id encodes the reference syntax at the use-site while node.kind normalizes to the resolved category 'external_symbol'. Consumer-facing question: document as expected, or normalize the id kind-slot. The route/event role-disagreement portion (id kind-slot encoding a ROLE the kind field does not carry: route->function 8, event_subscriber->function 11, event_publisher->function 3) was a distinct producer bug, split out to WI-kugaj (over-fold reconciliation). RELATED_BUT_DISTINCT from INV-dulah (id FORMAT escaping the 5-segment shape), parent META INV-kurup, and F100.A1/WI-vuzaf (id NAME-segment vs node.name). Blind severity 3/5 (pre-split); the external_symbol-only remainder may warrant demotion as arguably-expected."  # f646
